{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Before the priest comes, etc.</b> For as long as a priest has not attended to it, there is no law of impurity." "<b>And he shall not contaminate all that is in the house.</b> For if he does not empty it out and the priest comes and sees the plague and declares it quarantined, everything inside it becomes impure. And what does the Torah spare? If it is wooden vessels, he immerses them and they become pure; and if it is foods and liquids, he eats them during his days of impurity — thus the Torah spares none but earthen vessels, which have no purification in the mikveh (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:28.293155164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}